  "title": "Extension complexity of (convex) polygons",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "The extension complexity of a polytope $P$ is the minimum number $q$ for which there exists a polytope $Q$ with $q$ facets and an affine mapping $\\pi$ with $\\pi(Q) = P$.\n\nQuestion Does there exists, for infinitely many integers $n$, a convex polygon on $n$ vertices whose extension complexity is $\\Omega(n)$?",
